\"windows | linux\",\n    \"description\": \"Comprehensive overview of what this playbook does\",\n    \"confidence_score\": 0.95,\n    \"confidence_level\": \"High\",\n    \"confidence_reason\": \"All actions mapped directly to registered platform tools with complete parameter schemas and high procedural fidelity.\",\n    \"required_entities\": [\"user_id\", \"email\", \"hostname\"],\n    \"trigger_words\": [\"unlock\", \"account\", \"login\", \"platform_name\"],\n    \"steps\": [\n        {{\n            \"step_number\": 1,\n            \"sop_step_description\": \"Detailed step objective\",\n            \"step_type\": \"tool_call | command\",\n            \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 result and why tool_call/command was chosen; why this exact platform/function/command and comm_inputs/placeholders were used over alternatives.\",\n            \"platform\": \"platform name from REGISTERED API TOOLS CATALOG (only for tool_call, else null)\",\n            \"function_name\": \"exact_function_name (from REGISTERED API TOOLS CATALOG above, only for tool_call, else null)\",\n            \"comm_inputs\": {{\n                \"user_id\": \"{{{{entities.user_id}}}}\"\n            }},\n            \"command\": \"ipconfig /all (only for command, else null)\",\n            \"shell\": \"powershell (only for command, else null)\",\n            \"fallback_command\": null,\n            \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n            \"expected_output_contains\": \"unlocked\",\n            \"timeout_seconds\": 30,\n            \"output_variable\": \"step_result\",\n            \"output_parse_instruction\": \"Inspect output/JSON response and set status flags.\",\n            \"execute_if\": null,\n            \"is_dangerous\": false,\n            \"danger_warning\": null\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n```\n\n## RAW SOP DOCUMENT TEXT TO TRANSLATE:\nSOP-L1-APP-001\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\nSTANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE\n\nSoftware Application Unblock\n\nRequest\n\nEndpoint Support  →  Application Management\n\nSOP ID\nSOP-L1-APP-001\n\nSupport Level\nL1 Service Desk\n\nCategory\nEndpoint Support / Application Management\n\nPrimary Remediation Path\nIFEO Debugger Entry Removal\n\nDocument Version\n1.0\n\nStatus\nApproved for Use\n\nClassification\nInternal Use Only\n\nThis document defines the standard, command-based process for identifying an\napplication block caused by an Image File Execution Options (IFEO) debugger entry\n\nand removing it as a fallback remediation on a Windows endpoint.\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\nPage 1\n\nSOP-L1-APP-001\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\n.  Table of Contents\n\n1.\nObjective\n\n2.\nPreconditions\n\n3.\nProcess Flow Overview\n\n4.\nDetailed Procedure\n\nStep 1 — Verify Endpoint Connectivity\n\nStep 2 — Identify Application Blocking Mechanism\n\nStep 3 — Remove IFEO Block (Fallback)\n\nStep 4 — Refresh Local Policy\n\nStep 5 — Verify Block Removal\n\nStep 6 — Validate Resolution\n\nStep 7 — Update Ticket\n\n5.\nEscalation Criteria\n\n6.\nDocument Control\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\nPage 2\n\nSOP-L1-APP-001\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\n1.  Objective\n\nRestore access to an approved software application that is blocked on a Windows endpoint by identifying the\nblocking mechanism and applying the appropriate remediation. If the block is caused by an Image File\nExecution Options (IFEO) debugger entry, remove the entry as a fallback remediation.\n\n2.  Preconditions\n\n•\nTicket assigned to L1 Engineer.\n\n•\nRemote administrative access to the endpoint.\n\n•\nUser device is online.\n\n•\nAdministrative privileges available.\n\n3.  Process Flow Overview\n\nThe diagram below summarizes the end-to-end decision flow. Full instructions for each stage are provided in\nSection 4, Detailed Procedure.\n\n1. Verify\nConnectivity\n→\n2. Identify Blocking\nMechanism\n→\n3–5. Remove, Refresh\n& Verify\n\nIs the application blocked via an IFEO Debugger entry? (Step 2)\n\nYES — IFEO Debugger Entry Found\nNO — Registry Key Not Found\n\nProceed to Step 3 — remove the Debugger entry\n(and the key itself if it exists solely to block the app),\nthen refresh policy and verify.\n\nApplication is not blocked through IFEO. Investigate\nAppLocker, WDAC, Intune, or Endpoint Security\npolicies, or escalate to L2.\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\nPage 3\n\nSOP-L1-APP-001\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\n4.  Detailed Procedure\n\nSTEP 1  —  Verify Endpoint Connectivity\n\nCommand\n\nTest-Connection <ComputerName> -Count 2\n\n\u0014 Expected Result: Reply received from target system.\n\nIf unreachable — Action:\n\n•\nVerify VPN / network connectivity.\n\n•\nRetry.\n\n•\nEscalate if unreachable.\n\nSTEP 2  —  Identify Application Blocking Mechanism\n\nCommand\n\nreg query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\"\n\nExpected Result 1\n\nDebugger    REG_SZ    ...\n\nResult: Application is blocked using IFEO. Proceed to Step 3.\n\nExpected Result 2\n\nERROR:\nThe system was unable to find the specified registry key.\n\nResult: Application is not blocked through IFEO. Investigate other blocking technologies (AppLocker, WDAC,\nIntune, Endpoint Security) or escalate to L2.\n\nSTEP 3  —  Remove IFEO Block (Fallback)\n\nExecute only when Step 2 confirms an IFEO Debugger entry.\n\nRemove Debugger Value\n\nreg delete \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\" ^\n  /v Debugger /f\n\nIf the application-specific IFEO key was created only for blocking, remove the key:\n\nreg delete \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\" ^\n  /f\n\nSTEP 4  —  Refresh Local Policy\n\nCommand\n\ngpupdate /force\n\n\u0014 Expected Result: Computer Policy update has completed successfully. User Policy update has completed\nsuccessfully.\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\nPage 4\n\nSOP-L1-APP-001\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\nSTEP 5  —  Verify Block Removal\n\nCommand\n\nreg query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\"\n\n\u0014 Expected Result: ERROR: The system was unable to find the specified registry key — or — Debugger\nvalue not present.\n\nSTEP 6  —  Validate Resolution\n\nAsk the user to launch the application.\n\n\u0014 Expected Result:\n\n•\nApplication launches successfully.\n\n•\nNo error message displayed.\n\n•\nUser confirms issue resolved.\n\nIf the application remains blocked:\n\n•\nCheck for AppLocker policies.\n\n•\nCheck WDAC policies.\n\n•\nCheck Endpoint Security policies.\n\n•\nEscalate to L2 Support.\n\nSTEP 7  —  Update Ticket\n\nResolution Notes\n\nIssue:\nApplication launch blocked.\n\nRoot Cause:\nIFEO Debugger registry entry prevented application execution.\n\nAction Taken:\nVerified IFEO configuration.\nRemoved Debugger registry entry.\nRefreshed Group Policy.\nValidated successful application launch.\n\nStatus:\nResolved.\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\nPage 5\n\nSOP-L1-APP-001\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\n5.  Escalation Criteria\n\nEscalate to L2 if:\n\n•\nIFEO key not present.\n\n•\nApplication blocked by WDAC.\n\n•\nApplication blocked by AppLocker.\n\n•\nEndpoint protection policy prevents execution.\n\n•\nRegistry modification fails.\n\n•\nUser lacks required permissions.\n\n•\nApplication still fails after remediation.\n\n6.  Document Control\n\nAttribute\nValue\n\nSOP ID\nSOP-L1-APP-001\n\nTitle\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\nCategory\nEndpoint Support → Application Management\n\nSupport Level\nL1 Service Desk\n\nPrimary Remediation Path\nIFEO Debugger Entry Removal\n\nVersion\n1.0\n\nStatus\nApproved for use\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\nPage 6"
